is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
I cannot reproduce the outage. Campus 1 networks are reachable from the rest of the network, and the Campus 1 edge (router16) is operating normally.

Evidence:
- End-to-end reachability is good: topology-wide tests show hosts across other sites (10.5.0.x, 10.6.0.x, etc.) can ping Campus 1 hosts 172.16.10.7/8 with 0% loss. Targeted tests from dc_pc5 to 172.16.20.10 and 172.16.30.12 also succeed with low latency, as does dc_pc5 to 172.16.10.5.
- Routing is correct: router7 (upstream) has OSPF routes to 172.16.10.0/24, 172.16.20.0/24, and 172.16.30.0/24 via 172.30.1.1 (router16). On router16, OSPF neighbors are Full on both uplinks: 192.168.10.1 over eth2 (172.30.1.2 peer) and 10.2.2.2 over bond0. Router16 can ping both neighbors directly.
- The Campus 1 edge interface eth2 (172.30.1.1/24) is up, and OSPF adjacencies are established; traffic forwards bidirectionally.

Mechanism if the reported symptom had occurred would be loss of OSPF adjacency or missing routes on router7 pointing to router16, but neither is observed.

Root cause: No current fault found; the issue is not reproducible.

Corrective fix: No action required at this time. Recommend monitoring router16’s OSPF and interfaces for flaps and reviewing logs if the problem reoccurs, but connectivity and routing are presently healthy. Please have users retest. 
=== END ===